{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/280619-odd-headcanons","id":280619,"title":"Odd Headcanons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-13T22:33:12-07:00","id":280619,"title":"Odd Headcanons","content":"I am not talking about ships, but what shows or movies or novels have you tried to fit together into one giant headcanon? For me, it is the Underworld movies along with Jumper and Push. What about the rest of you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:07:12-07:00","id":280657,"title":"","content":"Battlestar Galactica (2004), and the Sarah Conner Chronicles (and by extension the first two Terminator movies, as the SCC only builds on those two) occur in the same universe. All of this has happened before, and all of it shall happen again.<br /> <br /> After the machines are victorious in the Terminator era - the Matrix happens (which corresponds nicely to parallel Caprica).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:40:35-07:00","id":281042,"title":"","content":"Late Golden/Silver era DC comics with late Silver/Bronze era Marvel comics. There seemed to be some DC heroes that could act nicely as mentors for the up-and-coming Marvel heroes.<br /> <br /> One of the things that started this idea percolating was <b><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0147746/\" target=\"_blank\">Batman Beyond</a></b> because Terry McGinnis comes across more like Peter Parker than the next generation Bruce Wayne. Also, with the wrist-mounted grapplers, super-strength, and clinging to walls.....he's not too far away from Spider-Man. How he dealt with The Joker in <b>Return of the Joker</b> really cemented it for me. Add to this the nature of their villains. Batman's are usually street-level lunatics with a gimmick, which in many ways is taking exactly what Batman does (street-level vigilante using psychological techniques and technological gimmicks to scare criminals) and twisting it. Spider-Man &quot;fell into&quot; a sciency accident and decided to be responsible with the powers (after a harsh lesson in taking the alternative) and many of his villains also &quot;fell into&quot; a sciency accident, but decided to be greedy, selfish, or angry about it and take it out on everyone else (and often have their own psychological problems, too).<br /> <br /> So, I started trying to find some others characters who's style/attitude/niche seemed to meld. I didn't get very far in it, just a few. I thought &quot;finding America&quot; Green Arrow's liberal ideas of justice would go pretty well with Daredevil and his street-level vigilantism. Wonder Woman could help Thor learn to live as a god amongst men. Superman influencing Captain (Ms.) Marvel as a powerful, forthright hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I know, my inner geek is really showing with this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:14:37-07:00","id":281108,"title":"","content":"Let me tell you about my headcannon.<br /> <img src=\"http://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/new.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:24:23-07:00","id":281134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/280619-odd-headcanons?p=281108#post281108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me tell you about my headcannon.<br /> <img src=\"http://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/new.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of that one, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:20:16-07:00","id":281411,"title":"","content":"God-Machine is a shard of Void Dragon that made it into the universe of NWoD, hence it's supreme power over physics. <br /> <br /> Note that Adeptus Mechanicus worship another shard of Void Dragon under the guise of Machine God.<br /> <br /> Coincidence? I think not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{